  "rules": [
    "Static release allowlist only; an unknown id, version or target combination is INVALID.",
    "Target identity, target revision, communication id and source scope remain in CommunicationProposalEvidenceV1; they are not duplicated into the typed facts.",
    "Membership proposals target the governing FAULT_TAG in the envelope and carry one exact membership identity/revision; LLD-07 verifies current parent-tag membership plus obligation/unit authority.",
    "facts is passed without modification to the exact Inventory owner payload validator. Rejected decision reason must already be normalized, be nonempty, have no NUL/CR/LF and occupy at most 384 UTF-8 bytes.",
    "Source messages, subjects, bodies, participants, attachment names/bytes, opaque parser handles, filesystem paths and proof/session material are forbidden in proposal payloads and diagnostic/audit copies.",
    "Extraction never invents a lifecycle fact from the presence of an identifier or a keyword. Missing or ambiguous facts stay unresolved and no actionable domain-fact proposal is generated.",
    "Submission evidence requires a retained canonical SENT communication; a draft, MSG export, UNKNOWN/RECEIVED direction or filename cannot satisfy indexed_sent.",
    "Domain-fact acceptance creates no communication link by implication; pending/deferred proposals have active PROPOSAL protection holds.",
    "One owning command boundary/receipt and caller UnitOfWork; validate Communication evidence and all owner freshness first, perform the owner mutation, record accepted Communication disposition and close its hold, evaluate retention, persist audits/exact replay result, commit atomically.",
    "Any provider, owner, disposition, audit or result failure rolls back all database effects. Replay returns the immutable original result before current-state/provider reads.",
    "Warehouse final decision retains the owning explicit_confirmation=true requirement; proposal evidence never supplies that confirmation.",
    "Every Communications membership proposal has one proposed membership fact. One message can produce independent proposals; any owning Inventory proposal/batch remains all-target atomic under its existing acceptance contract.",
    "No new LLD-03 or LLD-05 domain-fact mutation contract is created by this candidate. Their targets support link proposals; evidence/disposition interfaces remain available for a future separately accepted owner mapping.",
    "The other LLD-07 proposal kinds retain the pinned unsupported-acceptance rule until an exact new typed owner mapping is accepted.",
    "Fingerprint authority and semantic extraction rules require the accompanying reconciliation text before runtime registration."
  ],
  "accepted_at": "2026-09-30",
